  "worked_solution": "First, we find the smallest and largest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- There is no smallest $y$-value.\n\n- The largest $y$-value is $3.$ This occurs when $x=0.$\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-\\infty $ and $3,$ including $3.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-\\infty <y\\le 3,$ which can also be written as  $-\\infty <f(x)\\le 3.$",
